<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">heal</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">heal</ansi> shows who in your company is hurt: their health, their wound
limit, their wounds, and what would help. It changes nothing.

<ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi> tends the company after a fight. You never name a healer or
a patient; it goes in this order:

  1. <ansi fg="yellow">The clerics.</ansi> Every member with you who knows Tend Wounds or Minor
     Heal and has mana, the most mana first, treats the most hurt first
     (wounds before plain damage). Each tends every wound (4 mana, 2 to 6
     points closed), then heals up to the wound limit (Minor Heal, 3 mana,
     10 to 16 health plus 1 for every 6 levels of the healer, 5% more
     with a holy symbol), until the mana runs out. This takes no time: the mana
     is spent, but there are no chants.
  2. <ansi fg="yellow">The packs.</ansi> Then birch splints go on each broken bone (4 points
     each) and linen bandages on each cut or puncture (3 points each),
     one after another until the wound closes or they run out. A bandage is
     also wrapped round anyone still under half their limit (3 health).
     They come from the cargo first, then the patient's own pack, then yours,
     then the others'.
  3. <ansi fg="yellow">A physician.</ansi> Where there is one (the Waymark Inn in Dunmar), the
     physician offers to close every wound left for a price per wound, and
     asks <ansi fg="command">Pay 30 gold? [yes/no]</ansi>. Only yes pays; if you can't afford
     it, you're told so instead.
  4. The report: who is still hurt, and whether a rest would help.

It can't be used in a fight: your healers heal during a fight by their
strategy (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). An inn stay closes whatever is left; a camp
rest closes a broken bone for each splint, and a cut or puncture for each
bandage, you carry (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>).

After every battle your clerics already heal the hurt up to your healing
threshold, keeping their mana reserve (<ansi fg="command">help patch</ansi>); <ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi> goes
further, to the wound limit, and spends every drop. Out of a fight,
everyone also recovers slowly on their own while you're logged in, but
only up to half their health; companions keep their health between
sessions (<ansi fg="command">help readiness</ansi>).

Clerics can also cast the spells by hand: <ansi fg="command">cast heal [who]</ansi> and
<ansi fg="command">cast tend [who]</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>).

Group healing reaches your present company without a player party. A chant
rechecks life, presence and ownership, and healing stops at wound limits
(<ansi fg="command">help friendly-effects</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">heal</ansi>           who is hurt, and what would help
  <ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi>    tend the company after a fight

See also: <ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>.
